invariant: INV-36
file: test/zig-consumer/matches.zig
catches: test/zig-build-check.sh
reason: matches.zig's reverse check refuses the functions the object does
  provide instead of the ones it lacks. A check that read no declaration
  would pass this edit, so a failure here is what shows the walk over
  chapulin.c runs the comparison: the default object's ch_connect stops
  matches.zig from compiling.

--- old
        if (!provided(decl.name)) @compileError("chapulin.c declares " ++ decl.name ++ ", which the object neither exports nor imports");
--- new
        if (provided(decl.name)) @compileError("chapulin.c declares " ++ decl.name ++ ", which the object neither exports nor imports");
